Independent code and security review
- Independent C19 code review completed with no blocking findings. The reviewer confirmed authorization-before-lookup on write paths, `run:read` read gates, workspace compound SQL topology, 0010 hardening triggers, live Mission Control API projection, and no static-fixture-only Gateway page.
- Independent C19 security review completed with no blocking findings. The reviewer confirmed cross-workspace existence-oracle coverage, RBAC/scope exact matching, SQL parameterization, service/repository/DB allowlist default-deny, append-only message/delivery triggers, HttpOnly local-session bootstrap, explicit workspace alias handling, and no real external provider/MCP side effects.
- Residual non-blocking risks recorded for later stages: DB-level `secret://` checks are looser than contract schemas, loopback detection is syntactic, local bearer claims have no embedded expiry/audience beyond cookie lifetime/secret rotation, the Gateway UI currently picks the first gateway descriptor, and future real provider receipt refs/error messages must be sanitized before storage.

Code and security spot checks
- C19 inputs parse through Zod strict schemas; reads require `run:read`; writes require owner/admin scope; update/session commands require `If-Match`; idempotency conflicts return 409; exact idempotent replays return the original accepted object.
- Gateway/channel/session/message/delivery/allowlist facts are workspace scoped; delivery receipts and messages are append-only; cursor checkpoints reject stale progress and allow fully identical replays.
- Outbound message send defaults to deny without an active allowlist entry; denied sends create no delivery receipt and do not perform network calls.
- Client-facing schema errors are generic and do not echo synthetic secret/token/internal-path values used by tests.

Environment limitations
- TypeScript/YAML LSP servers are not installed in this workspace; verification relied on `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, focused/full tests, smoke checks, browser screenshots, and source review.
- Browser QA used the locally available Playwright/browser setup through the manual runner. Fresh PNG dimensions and DOM observations were recorded in the summary JSON and verified with `file`.
